package CanvasNet {
    part def SpecNormalizer {
        doc /* The internal static partial SpecNormalizer with the LayerTree, LayerNode, LayerResolve, ResolveMode, ExpandedLayers, CompositeAxis, and CompositeBuilder types: it reduces the views of a parsed specification to the tree of unit views that are drawn, so that every later stage draws unit views and needs no special case for layers or composite marks. Layers(tree, limits) builds the LayerTree with an explicit stack: a specification without layer is one unit view, the root itself, so a single view takes the path it always took; the objects of a layer array are the layers of a layered view (unit views or layered views, to any depth); a view that holds a concat, hconcat, vconcat, facet, or repeat is recorded as a composition that is not drawn yet and is not entered. A layer inherits as in Vega-Lite: the encoding of the layered views above it (the outermost first, a channel of an inner view replacing the outer channel in place and a new channel added after the existing ones, as a node that is not adopted by its parent so every pointer, line, and column stays that of the specification), the width and height of the top-level view, and, as the view's own, the data and the transform that the document applies down the tree (the transform of a layered view first); the resolve of each layered view is read into a LayerResolve (shared scales by default, the axis and legend of an independent scale independent). MaxViews (every view, the views of an expansion included) and MaxCompositionDepth (the nesting of layer) fail closed with a located VegaLiteRenderException at the exact limit. Expand(tree, config, limits) replaces a unit view whose mark is boxplot, errorbar, or errorband by a layered view of the primitive layers that Vega-Lite normalizes it to, written as synthetic nodes located at the mark, with the expressions it writes compiled into a derived specification tree: a boxplot as the outlier points, the whiskers (rules and optional end ticks over the values inside the fences, or from the minimum to the maximum for min-max), and the box with its median tick, with the defaults of config.boxplot; an errorbar from raw observations (the stderr, stdev, ci, or iqr extent around the mean or median), a pre-aggregated range, or errors, as a rule with optional ticks; an errorband as a rect (one dimension) or an area (two dimensions) with optional rule or line borders; the part switches, part properties, orientation, grouping channels, and titles follow Vega-Lite, and an orientation or encoding that cannot be decided is a VegaLiteSpecException at the mark. The unit performs no file or network access and holds no state; the expansion rules are ported from Vega-Lite compositemark with attribution (the files carry the provenance header). */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecNormalizer.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecNormalizer.Composite.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecNormalizer.BoxPlot.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite/SpecModel/SpecNormalizer.ErrorBar.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecNormalizerTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecNormalizerBoxPlotTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.VegaLite.Tests/SpecModel/SpecNormalizerErrorBarTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-normalizer.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-normalizer.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-vega-lite/spec-model/spec-normalizer.yaml */
    }
}
